      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The provided analyses indicate that the most important spaces in a pair of Virginia-class attack boats are the control room modules, hatches, chairs, terminals, doors, desks, screens, outlets, fixtures, lightbulbs, and chart tables. These spaces are crucial for the operation and functionality of the control room, which is the central hub of the submarine. The control room is essential for managing navigation, communication, and other critical functions. Without these spaces, the submarine would be unable to operate effectively, and the crew would be unable to perform their duties.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
